---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { corrections, formatDate } from "../lib/data";

/**
 * The corrections log.
 *
 * Three pages promised this before it existed. That is exactly the kind of
 * claim this project exists to catch other people making, so it is either true
 * or the sentence comes off the pages.
 *
 * An empty log is a real claim, not an absence: it says nothing has needed
 * correcting since the date given, and anyone can test that against the
 * repository history. It is published rather than hidden until there is
 * something in it.
 */
const rows = corrections();
const FIRST_PUBLISHED = "2026-09-01";
const REPO = "https://github.com/toohardbasket-lab/toohardbasket";
---

<Base
  title="Corrections"
  description="Every correction made to this site since it was published, and how to report one."
>
  <section class="wrap measure">
    <p class="eyebrow">Corrections</p>
    <h1>Corrections</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      This site publishes figures drawn from parliamentary records. When one of them is
      wrong, the useful thing is to fix it quickly and leave a visible record that it was
      fixed.
    </p>

    <h2>How to report one</h2>
    <p>
      Write to{" "}
      <a href="mailto:corrections@toohardbasket.org.au">corrections@toohardbasket.org.au</a>{" "}
      with the row or figure you think is wrong and, if you have it, the source that shows
      it. You do not need to be certain; a question is enough.
    </p>

    <h2>What happens then</h2>
    <p>
      A correction is made within 24 hours of being confirmed, and listed below with the
      date, what changed, and the record that settled it. If you reported it and would like
      to be named, say so and you will be; otherwise the entry says nothing about who
      raised it.
    </p>
    <p>
      Underneath the list there is a second record: every change to the data and to these
      pages is a commit in the {" "}<a href={REPO}>public repository</a>, with a timestamp
      and an explanation. The list below is a plain-English index of the corrections in that
      history, not a substitute for it.
    </p>
    <p>
      That history has been rewritten twice: on 28 August 2026, when the repository was
      recreated, and on 1 September 2026, to remove internal planning notes that should
      never have been committed to a public repository. No data and no page content was
      changed on either occasion, and it has not been rewritten since.
    </p>
    <p>
      A figure moving is not the same as a correction. Both registers rebuild from their
      source documents, and the count changes when a government response is tabled or a
      presiding officer publishes a new schedule. Those movements are not listed here; only
      errors are.
    </p>

    <h2 id="log">The log</h2>
    {rows.length === 0 ? (
      <p class="empty">
        <strong>No corrections have been made since this site was published on
        {" "}{formatDate(FIRST_PUBLISHED)}.</strong>{" "}
        The repository history shows every change made since then and why.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <ol class="log">
        {rows.map((r) => (
          <li>
            <p class="head">
              <span class="when">{formatDate(r.date)}</span>
              <span class="where">{r.page}</span>
            </p>
            <p class="what">{r.what}</p>
            <p class="src">
              <span class="k">Source</span> {r.source}
              {r.reportedBy && <><span class="k">Reported by</span> {r.reportedBy}</>}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    )}

    <h2>Errors found before publication</h2>
    <p>
      Several were. They are in the repository history, not in the list above, because
      nothing published to this site carried them. The largest: the Senate register was
      originally built by treating every report on the President's report as though it were
      still awaiting a response. Her report is not a list of outstanding responses; it is a
      status list, with a column recording which reports have been answered. Reading that
      column properly removed about 150 reports that had in fact been answered. The error
      was found and fixed before the register was published.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  h2 { margin-top: 2.25rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; }
  .empty {
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  /*
   * A correction is a paragraph, not a cell. In a four-column table inside a
   * single measure column the explanation was squeezed into a two-word ribbon,
   * which read as a broken page rather than as a record. Each correction is a
   * block: when and where at the top, what changed in full, and the record
   * that settled it underneath.
   */
  .log { list-style: none; margin: 1.25rem 0 0; padding: 0; }
  .log > li {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 1.1rem 0 1.2rem;
  }
  .log > li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .log .head {
    margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
    display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.25rem 1rem; align-items: baseline;
  }
  .log .when {
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; font-weight: 600; font-size: 0.9375rem;
  }
  .log .where {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }
  .log .what { margin: 0; line-height: 1.6; }
  .log .src {
    margin: 0.6rem 0 0; font-size: 0.875rem; line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--ink-secondary);
  }
  .log .src .k {
    font-size: 0.6875rem; letter-spacing: 0.09em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted); margin-right: 0.35rem;
  }
  .log .src .k:not(:first-child) { margin-left: 0.9rem; }
  .cmte { color: var(--ink-secondary); font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
  .who { display: block; font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--ink-muted); }
</style>
